          "question": "my dads left arm has gone all achy n hes gone grey and sweaty, hes 62, is that somethin to worry about",
          "answer": "**Call emergency services now. Do not wait to see if it passes.**\n\nThe urgency tool returned \"routine\" because none of its fixed rules matched that wording. I'm not following that result, because it doesn't fit what you describe. The guidance on chest pain says discomfort spreading to one or both arms, or chest discomfort with cold sweat, is treated as a possible heart attack until proven otherwise (*Chest pain that may indicate a heart attack*, emergency medicine and cardiology guidance). Your dad has new arm ache, greyness and sweating, which matches that pattern.\n\nUntil help arrives:\n- Keep him sitting or lying still. Do not let him walk around or drive himself.\n- Loosen tight clothing and keep him calm.\n- Tell the call handler exactly what you've seen and when it started.\n- Tell them if his face droops, his speech slurs, or he loses strength in an arm or leg. The stroke guidance (*Sudden neurological symptoms that may indicate a stroke*) also says to call immediately for these signs.\n- If he becomes unresponsive or stops breathing normally, follow the instructions the call handler gives you.\n\nEven if the symptoms ease, he still needs to be checked urgently. Better to have a false alarm than a missed heart attack.\n\nNot medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.",
